schema-version 1

description "NVIDIA in a virtio-nvgpu guest: the virtio_gpu_nv kernel driver, built against the image kernel, which presents the host GPU as /dev/nvidia*. NVIDIA's userspace (GL, EGL, Vulkan, NVENC) comes from hardware/nvidia without its kernel modules, at the host driver's release."

supports "fedora"

requires "build-environment"
requires "kernel-devel"
requires "nvidia-driver"

provides "nvidia-kmod" file="/usr/lib/virtio-nvgpu/installed"

// The stub replaces the nvidia-modprobe that NVIDIA's packages install.
mode "/usr/bin/nvidia-modprobe" "0755"
